<title>POLAND: Polish credit,deposit rates seen flat in H1-survey.</title>
<headline>Polish credit,deposit rates seen flat in H1-survey.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish bankers expect credit and deposit rates in commercial banks to hold flat until the end of July and to fall slightly at the end of 1997, according to a monthly poll by the Dziennik Prawa i Gospodarki business daily.</p>
<p>				 Now    July '97    End '97    June '98</p>
<p> Call deposits (pct)    10.7     10.7	  10.3	  9.9</p>
<p> 3-month depos	    17.44    17.44	 16.5	 14.8</p>
<p> 6-month depos	    18.4     18.4	  17.3	 15.8</p>
<p> 12-month depos	   19.5     19.5	  18.3	 16.8</p>
<p> Corporate credit*	23.94    23.94	 23.1	 21.6</p>
<p> Consumer credit*	 26.1     26.1	  24.9	 23.5</p>
<p>NOTE: Corporate credit base rate is given, consumer credit for a period of 12 months. The survey was conducted among about a dozen large Polish banks, the daily said.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
